<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating patient selection for a study of inpatients diagnosed with type two diabetes mellitus, showing inclusion and exclusion criteria, leading to 766 patients enrolled, and dividing into sarcopenia and non-sarcopenia groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Nine grouped bar charts compare prevalence percentages of sarcopenia and severe sarcopenia according to indices SII, SIRI, NLR, PIV, PLR, NPAR, NLPR, PNR, HRR, and ALI, across tertiles T1, T2, and T3. Higher tertiles generally show increased prevalence. P-values indicate statistical significance for trends in most charts.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Figure containing two panels, A and B, each with multiple line graphs displaying odds ratio with confidence intervals \(shaded region\) for different biomarkers including SII, SIRI, NLR, PLR, NPAR, NLPR, PNR, PV, HBR, and ALI. Each plot shows a positive or non-linear association between biomarker values and odds ratio. P-values for trend and nonlinearity are indicated above each graph, demonstrating statistical assessment for each relationship. Panel A and Panel B contain similar sets of biomarkers with slight variations in plotted relationships and P-values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Two line charts display net benefit versus threshold probability, each comparing three strategies: None \(black solid line\), All \(gray solid line\), and ALI \(black dashed line\). ALI shows higher net benefit than the other strategies at lower threshold probabilities in both charts.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
